1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--speaking-analysis","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/speaking-analysis","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/speaking-analysis","sourceHash":"ad1eccea2099b7f52feed6baa422427e33ffc9e40167b4d577de124162b201b6","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T23:11:04.895Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Speaking Analysis","zh":"口语分析"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Speaking analysis means recording yourself speaking and then going back to analyze what you said. It separates the act of speaking (which requires real-time processing) from the act of analyzing (which requires careful attention) — and doing them separately makes both more effective.","zh":"口语分析是指录下自己说话的内容，然后回过头来分析自己说了什么。它将说话（需要实时处理）与分析（需要仔细关注）分开进行，从而让两者都更有效。"}},{"id":"how-to-do-it","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"How to Do It","zh":"具体做法"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"en":"Record yourself speaking — a monologue, a reading, or even a conversation (with permission)","zh":"录下自己的口语——可以是独白、朗读，甚至是对话（需征得对方同意）"},{"en":"Listen back and note errors: wrong words, incorrect grammar, pronunciation issues, awkward phrasing","zh":"回听录音并记录错误：用词错误、语法不正确、发音问题以及表达不自然之处"},{"en":"Identify patterns — do you make the same type of mistake repeatedly?","zh":"找出规律——你是否反复犯同一类错误？"},{"en":"Target those patterns in your study","zh":"在学习中有针对性地改进这些问题"}]},{"id":"methods","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Methods","zh":"方法"}},{"id":"segment-0005","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>Self-analysis:</strong> Simply listen to your recording and make notes. This builds your ability to hear your own mistakes — a skill that eventually transfers to real-time self-monitoring during conversation.","zh":"<strong>自我分析：</strong>直接听自己的录音并做笔记。这样可以培养你听出自身错误的能力，而这项能力最终会迁移到对话中的实时自我监控。"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>With a tutor:</strong> Play the recording during a lesson and have your tutor point out errors and explain corrections. This gives you expert feedback and deeper insight into what's wrong. You can also discuss corrections and alternate phrasings to learn more.","zh":"<strong>与导师一起分析：</strong>在课程中播放录音，请导师指出错误并解释如何改正。这样可以获得专业反馈，并更深入地了解问题所在。你还可以讨论修改方案和其他表达方式，从中学到更多。"}},{"id":"segment-0007","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"<strong>AI-assisted:</strong> Use an AI transcription tool to transcribe your audio, then feed the transcript into a writing corrector or AI chatbot. Words the AI transcribes incorrectly probably indicate pronunciation problems. Grammar errors in the transcript reveal patterns you can study.","zh":"<strong>AI 辅助：</strong>使用 AI 转写工具将音频转换成文字，再把转写稿输入写作纠错工具或 AI 聊天机器人。AI 转写错误的单词很可能说明你的发音存在问题。转写稿中的语法错误则能揭示你可以针对性学习的错误模式。"}},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"建议"}},{"id":"segment-0009","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"Hearing your own voice in a foreign language feels weird. You'll get over it. And the analysis is worth the discomfort.","zh":"听到自己用外语说话的声音会感觉很奇怪，但你会习惯的。这种分析值得你忍受一时的不适。"},{"en":"Focus on patterns, not individual errors. If you make the same mistake 5 times, that's one thing to fix, not 5 separate problems.","zh":"关注错误规律，而不是单个错误。如果同一个错误犯了 5 次，那是一个需要解决的问题，而不是 5 个不同的问题。"},{"en":"<strong>Don't try to fix everything at once</strong>. Pick your 2-3 most common error types and work on those.","zh":"<strong>不要试图一次改正所有问题</strong>。选出最常见的 2～3 类错误，集中加以改进。"}]},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0011","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Speaking analysis is introduced in Phase 5C and continues through Phase 7.","zh":"口语分析会在阶段 5C 引入，并持续到阶段 7。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
